
PKG_CPPFLAGS=-I../inst/include

## g++-16 when using optimization appears to create code that creates
## segfaults for the linear regression and quadratic expression
## examples. Adding -fno-inline also helps. This appears to be limited
## to -O3; using -O2 or lower works. Using clang++ also works.
##
## Now, under CRAN Policies we cannot add either one of `-fno-inline`
## or `-O2` (or lower) here as "not portable".  We can however set
## `-g0` so we do.
##
## This also carries a tag which `tools/configure.R` replaces with
## '-Wno-ignored-attributes' (on "local" builds) to render the
## compilation a little more quiet
PKG_CXXFLAGS=@XTRAFLAGS@ -g0
